nd New Guinea were one. The second began to arrive from Europe at the end of the eighteenth century. Each had to come to terms with the land they found, and each had to make sense of the other. The long Aboriginal occupation of Australia witnessed spectacular changes. The rising of the seas isolated the continent and preserved a nomadic way of life, while agriculture was revolutionising other parts of the world. Over millennia, the Aboriginal people mastered the land's climates, seasons and resources. Traditional Aboriginal life came under threat the moment Europeans crossed the world to plant a new society in an unknown land. That land in turn rewarded, tricked, tantalised and often defeated the new arrivals.","thumbnailUrl":"https://books.google.com/books/content?id=r3fboQEACAAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&source=gbs_api","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":35,"criticalRenown":58,"controversy":18,"llmAffinity":78,"affinityResidual":2.19,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.78,"controversy":0.72,"llmAffinity":0.88},"tags":{"craft":"narrative-drive","evidence":"synthesis-of-scholarship","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"displaySummary":"The vast continent of Australia was settled in two main streams, far apart in time and origin. The first came ashore some 50,000 years ago when the islands of Australia, Tasmania and New Guinea were one. The second began to arrive from Europe at the end of the eighteenth century. Each had to come to terms with the land they found, and each had to make sense of the other. The long Aboriginal occupation of Australia witnessed spectacular changes. The rising of the seas isolated the continent and preserved a nomadic way of life, while agriculture was revolutionising other parts of the world. Over millennia, the Aboriginal people mastered the land's climates, seasons and resources. Traditional Aboriginal life came under threat the moment Europeans crossed the world to plant a new society in an unknown land. That land in turn rewarded, tricked, tantalised and often defeated the new arrivals.","primarySubject":"History","primaryTopic":"Energy, Extraction & Resources","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":12,"evidenceCount":4}],"evidence":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"History of australia","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey-2"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Economic history","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey-3"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Oceania, history","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-story-of-australia-s-people-the-rise-and-fall-of-ancient-australia-geoffrey-blainey-4"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Arts & Criticism","mappedSubject":"Arts & Criticism"